Short Story: Title: The Midnight Visitor
In a quiet village nestled between towering mountains, 
a lone traveler arrived just before midnight. His boots were worn, 
his cloak tattered, and his eyes tired, but determined. 
The townsfolk whispered tales of a hidden treasure deep within the valley, 
one that no one had ever dared to seek. The traveler, with a knowing smile, 
entered the local tavern and placed an ancient map on the bar. "Tomorrow," 
he said softly, "I shall find what has been lost for centuries."